      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventionally fabricated AlCrFeNiSi tends to undergo elemental segregation during cooling.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventionally fabricated AlCrFeNiSi retains high residual stresses and defect populations.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled high-energy mechanical alloying can produce atomistic mixing of the AlCrFeNiSi constituents.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pressure-assisted solid-state SPS can fully densify the alloy without melting it.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6385271::web::002::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A short SPS dwell time will minimize thermal gradients.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical alloying followed by SPS will produce a homogenized, ultrafine microstructure with uniform elemental distribution.",
